            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of tremor - deep brain stimulation as remedy for severe cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1850-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Tremor is a common motor disorder, in many diseases. Healthy persons may have low-amplitude physiological action tremor without any functional handicap, contrary to the disabling pathologic tremor. There are numerous types of tremor, and their etiology is poorly known. Tremor can at best be alleviated by drug therapy, but the response may abate with time. Deep brain stimulation has recently been increasingly utilized in the treatment of drug-resistant tremor in various neurologic diseases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
